{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2646 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "72cb0e58c7b0c6df740e19f6c072fae735bb44f1cc0b3a6f4f800f6e91c607c8" :edb/db-before-t 2645 :edb/db-after-t 2646 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535958 50 #inst "2026-10-09T11:34:59.002Z" 13194139535958 true] [17592186147387 1020 #edb/ref 17592186376596 13194139535958 true] [17592186147388 1020 #edb/ref 17592186376582 13194139535958 true] [17592186147388 1020 #edb/ref 17592186376603 13194139535958 true] [17592186147389 1020 #edb/ref 17592186376610 13194139535958 true] [17592186147390 1020 #edb/ref 17592186376589 13194139535958 true] [17592186376582 1017 #edb/ref 17592186376583 13194139535958 true] [17592186376582 1089 "q-64600" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376582 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535958 true] [17592186376582 1100 "A particle of mass $3\\,\\text{kg}$ is attached to a massless spring. The spring constant associated with the spring is $k=12\\,{\\text{kg/s}}^{2}.$  The particle is also subject to the resistive force that's proportional to the particle's velocity with a damping coefficient $c=9\\,\\text{kg/s},$ and an external force given by $F(t)=15\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,\\text{N}.$   \n\nThe position of the particle is $y(t)$ (measured in meters), and $t>0$ is the time in seconds.  If the particle moves with forced harmonic motion, what is the governing equation?" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376582 1113 #uuid "0f27aa5d-1895-501d-94c1-b1e7c835ede1" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376582 1145 "The general equation of forced harmonic motion with damping is\n\n$$\nm{y}^{″}=-c{y}^{′}-ky+F(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $m,$ $k,$ $c$ and $F(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n3{y}^{″}=-9{y}^{′}-12y+15\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\n$$\n\nSimplifying and rearranging the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+4y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\n$$" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376584 13194139535958 true] [17592186376583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376585 13194139535958 true] [17592186376583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376586 13194139535958 true] [17592186376583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376587 13194139535958 true] [17592186376583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376588 13194139535958 true] [17592186376583 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535958 true] [17592186376583 1041 "selection" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376583 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376585 13194139535958 true] [17592186376583 1110 #uuid "73e122ad-de35-50db-9d5a-999f0e97c8a1" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376584 1034 "{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+3y=15\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376584 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376584 1111 #uuid "013bf829-6d33-5fcc-8bba-b99d51c60713" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376585 1034 "{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+4y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376585 1111 #uuid "52d59049-6070-521d-8696-293de1bec4ca" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376586 1034 "{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+3y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376586 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376586 1111 #uuid "7977262c-2a7d-571a-bfa7-5236fa821be0" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376587 1034 "{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+2y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376587 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376587 1111 #uuid "f0bf89ae-11f6-5131-b017-01c2bd68e13e" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376588 1034 "{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+2y=15\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376588 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376588 1111 #uuid "9201ed99-6036-5d7e-83ab-140ac9a3d798" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376589 1017 #edb/ref 17592186376590 13194139535958 true] [17592186376589 1089 "q-64645" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376589 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535958 true] [17592186376589 1100 "The position $y(t),$ measured in meters, of a particle oscillating with forced harmonic motion with light damping is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+17y=40{e}^{-3t},\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. Given that the particle is initially at the origin with zero velocity, find the position of the particle after $\\pi $ second." 13194139535958 true] [17592186376589 1113 #uuid "79553835-e65f-59e1-aba2-8e979bcacb32" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376589 1145 "The general solution to the equation of forced harmonic motion with light damping is the sum of the complementary function and a particular solution.\n\nThe complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+17y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +17 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2} & =-16 \\\\ \\lambda +1 & =\\pm 4\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-1\\pm 4\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}={e}^{-t}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t).\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ and $Q$ are arbitrary constants of integration.\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(t).$\n\nThe external force is an exponential force. The constant factor in the exponent is $-2$, which is not a root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular exponential solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {e}^{-3t},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant to be determined. \n\nSubstituting ${y}_{p}$ into the differential equation and equating coefficients gives $\\alpha =2.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=2{e}^{-3t},\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-t}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t)+2{e}^{-3t}.\n$$\n\nSince the particle is initially at the origin with zero velocity, the initial conditions are $y(0)=0$ and ${y}^{′}(0)=0.$\n\nSolving with these conditions for $P$ and $Q$ gives\n\n$$\nP=-2,\\,Q=1.\n$$\n\nSo our solution is\n\n$$\ny(t)={e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t)+2{e}^{-3t}.\n$$\n\nTo find the position of the particle after $\\pi $ seconds, we substitute into the equation $t=\\pi .$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\pi ) & ={e}^{-\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡4(\\pi )-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4(\\pi ))+2{e}^{-3\\pi } \\\\  & =2{e}^{-\\pi }({e}^{-2\\pi }-1)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376591 13194139535958 true] [17592186376590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376592 13194139535958 true] [17592186376590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376593 13194139535958 true] [17592186376590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376594 13194139535958 true] [17592186376590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376595 13194139535958 true] [17592186376590 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535958 true] [17592186376590 1041 "selection" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376590 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376593 13194139535958 true] [17592186376590 1110 #uuid "d02bcfdd-4a16-5c27-b0d6-8fa4cc1b1524" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376591 1034 "y(\\pi )=(2{e}^{-3\\pi }-3)\\,\\text{m}" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376591 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376591 1111 #uuid "91c780e1-ae5f-5238-81e6-aea0e0462c10" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376592 1034 "y(\\pi )={e}^{-\\pi }(3{e}^{-2\\pi }-2)\\,\\text{m}" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376592 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376592 1111 #uuid "9e9b10be-246b-5a09-a794-829084d36f68" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376593 1034 "y(\\pi )=2{e}^{-\\pi }({e}^{-2\\pi }-1)\\,\\text{m}" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376593 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376593 1111 #uuid "1adf96a0-5d6d-540d-a81e-ebbca61f89fe" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376594 1034 "y(\\pi )={e}^{-\\pi }(4{e}^{-2\\pi }-1)\\,\\text{m}" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376594 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376594 1111 #uuid "c474055e-f2dd-576f-a44c-e0046802f78d" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376595 1034 "y(\\pi )=2({e}^{-3\\pi }-4)\\,\\text{m}" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376595 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376595 1111 #uuid "c4008f26-87f9-57e4-ab37-cda241f60295" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376596 1017 #edb/ref 17592186376597 13194139535958 true] [17592186376596 1089 "q-94231" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376596 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535958 true] [17592186376596 1100 "The function $y(t)$ gives the position of a particle at time $t>0.$ Which of the following equations represents a situation in which the particle is undergoing forced harmonic motion without damping?" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376596 1113 #uuid "c2c5477c-8ea5-5f3e-8509-189eb35b8466" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376596 1145 "The general equation of forced harmonic motion without damping is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t).\n$$\n\nWe can see that the only equation that represents forced harmonic motion without damping is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+7y={e}^{-4t}+t.\n$$" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376598 13194139535958 true] [17592186376597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376599 13194139535958 true] [17592186376597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376600 13194139535958 true] [17592186376597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376601 13194139535958 true] [17592186376597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376602 13194139535958 true] [17592186376597 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535958 true] [17592186376597 1041 "selection" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376597 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376602 13194139535958 true] [17592186376597 1110 #uuid "a015714c-c91d-5147-9e40-91e18340795f" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376598 1034 "{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+4y={e}^{5t}" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376598 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376598 1111 #uuid "8dd066cf-7eb7-59dc-bb41-a2f5256d6ce5" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376599 1034 "{y}^{″}-25y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376599 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376599 1111 #uuid "a2d4c358-334b-51bf-bec6-6a5259d1b854" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376600 1034 "{y}^{″}+36y=0" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376600 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376600 1111 #uuid "7dbf490c-d109-5c08-b66b-12ae85b46f7d" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376601 1034 "{y}^{″}+\\pi {y}^{′}+2y=0" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376601 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376601 1111 #uuid "303e30dd-b69e-53a9-9d0d-258f01aa377c" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376602 1034 "{y}^{″}+7y={e}^{-4t}+t" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376602 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376602 1111 #uuid "b2a087c2-9112-5b94-847c-670d9810cb0d" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376603 1017 #edb/ref 17592186376604 13194139535958 true] [17592186376603 1089 "q-94233" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376603 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535958 true] [17592186376603 1100 "A particle of mass $8\\,\\text{kg}$ is attached to a massless spring. The spring constant associated with the spring is $k=10\\,{\\text{kg/s}}^{2}.$  The particle is also subject to the resistive force that's proportional to the particle's velocity with a damping coefficient $c=16\\,\\text{kg/s},$ and an external force given by $F(t)=4{t}^{2}\\,\\text{N}.$   \n\nThe position of the particle is $y(t)$ (measured in meters), and $t>0$ is the time in seconds.  If the particle moves with forced harmonic motion, what is the governing equation?" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376603 1113 #uuid "06c834d3-f655-589c-886c-ecaa57db3e34" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376603 1145 "The general equation of forced harmonic motion with damping is\n\n$$\nm{y}^{″}=-c{y}^{′}-ky+F(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $m,$ $k,$ $c$ and $F(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n8{y}^{″}=-16{y}^{′}-10y+4{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying and rearranging the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+\\frac{5}{4}y=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376604 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376605 13194139535958 true] [17592186376604 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376606 13194139535958 true] [17592186376604 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376607 13194139535958 true] [17592186376604 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376608 13194139535958 true] [17592186376604 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376609 13194139535958 true] [17592186376604 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535958 true] [17592186376604 1041 "selection" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376604 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376609 13194139535958 true] [17592186376604 1110 #uuid "bd4349e2-a0d1-5188-93fd-91e37f8b9c7c" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376605 1034 "{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}+5y=\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376605 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376605 1111 #uuid "5d5c7d27-eefb-5ad5-b5a7-3b2cd1d5b8e2" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376606 1034 "{y}^{″}+\\frac{5}{2}y=\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376606 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376606 1111 #uuid "63ced7a7-284f-5b82-b18a-3621942228ee" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376607 1034 "{y}^{″}+2y=4{t}^{2}" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376607 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376607 1111 #uuid "fab92e09-6d90-5451-acc1-ecc8a417570d" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376608 1034 "{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+4y=2{t}^{2}" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376608 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376608 1111 #uuid "1ca71f6e-9d97-5127-a4ea-0f2947efdffa" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376609 1034 "{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+\\frac{5}{4}y=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376609 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535958 true] [17592186376609 1111 #uuid "c2113a69-96dc-55aa-88e2-bf4b065207d5" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376610 1017 #edb/ref 17592186376611 13194139535958 true] [17592186376610 1089 "q-94382" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376610 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535958 true] [17592186376610 1100 "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+25y=24\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(25t+ϕ)+12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t+ϕ)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R$ and $ϕ$ are constants." 13194139535958 true] [17592186376610 1113 #uuid "ec54a4bc-6f62-5d4e-afc1-aa3f503d9658" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376610 1145 "The general solution to this equation is the sum of the complementary function and a particular solution.\n\nFirst, we find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(t),$ which is the solution to the simple harmonic motion equation ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.$ It can be written in three different forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=25\\,⟹\\,\\omega =5.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t$\n\nNext, we find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t).$ The particular solution is of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution into the differential equation and equating coefficients, we find that $\\alpha =1$ and $\\beta =0.$ So, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t+ϕ)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t+ϕ)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\nOnly III matches the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139535958 true] [17592186376611 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376612 13194139535958 true] [17592186376611 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376613 13194139535958 true] [17592186376611 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376614 13194139535958 true] [17592186376611 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376615 13194139535958 true] [17592186376611 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376616 13194139535958 true] [17592186376611 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535958 true] [17592186376611 1041 "selection" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376611 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376615 13194139535958 true] [17592186376611 1110 #uuid "7111d041-05c2-50e2-bd88-a7a14f0cc3ba" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376612 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376612 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535958 true] [17592186376612 1111 #uuid "bc86b80a-8b5d-5519-8259-9d636519c27d" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376613 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535958 true] [17592186376613 1111 #uuid "d1a62164-6cf3-502b-8661-5afa9e5a6b22" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376614 1034 "I only" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376614 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535958 true] [17592186376614 1111 #uuid "851de8ad-103b-5e46-a2f2-7e2457bf773e" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376615 1034 "III only" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376615 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535958 true] [17592186376615 1111 #uuid "4d483b17-6630-52d2-85b7-8f7a08611b9a" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376616 1034 "II only" 13194139535958 true] [17592186376616 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535958 true] [17592186376616 1111 #uuid "836cdf4c-fbda-5284-8900-fdfb6624cc00" 13194139535958 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-64600" 17592186376582 "q-64600/selection" 17592186376583 "q-64600/selection/08fb8a2e6b01d5240e2d0844f530f8da720f476fdd0314f92af421eefa1febd7" 17592186376584 "q-64600/selection/3077d81c05dcc6e